{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-01 limb (a) is satisfied on the face of the trip record: it carries a driver 'arrived' event for this trip at 2026-08-21T17:03:40+08:00, followed two seconds later by the platform's own wait_timer_started event at 17:03:42. There is no dispute that a recorded arrival exists for TRP-03101; the question is only whether the GPS corroborates it, which the next claims address.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-03101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Limb (b) is satisfied on the driver's own trace. The pickup zone class is STANDARD, so the arrival radius is 50 m, and the trace places the driver inside that radius at 17:03:40 - the very timestamp the 'arrived' event carries - with 42 qualifying in-radius fixes. The longest qualifying run begins at 17:03:40 and dwell_start_offset_sec is 0.0, so geofence entry and arrival marker coincide to the second and there is no interval between them to argue about.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-03101", "EV-TRIP-03101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.first_ts",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Limb (c) is satisfied with a wide margin. The effective in-geofence dwell is a single continuous run of 410 seconds, from 17:03:40 to 17:10:30, over 42 fixes at a 10 second cadence, against a free waiting period in force of 180 seconds read from trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec. The derived shortfall is -230 seconds, that is a 230 second surplus, and platform_policy.no_show_threshold_sec is null so no longer threshold has to be met.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-03101", "EV-TRIP-03101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.shortfall_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Limb (d) is satisfied. The trip record shows no boarding event and records termination by the driver at 17:10:32 under cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, which is one of the three codes limb (d) expressly recognises, and the termination falls well after the dwell limb (c) requires had elapsed (410 seconds of dwell had run by 17:10:30). The claim that the driver cancelled 'early' cannot be run against these timestamps.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-03101", "EV-GPS-03101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The arrival marker is true, not false, so POL-NS-05 has no purchase here. The 'arrived' tap at 17:03:40 coincides to the second with the first qualifying in-geofence fix, and the run that follows is a stationary in-geofence interval of 42 fixes covering 410 seconds - the driver was at the pin and holding, not in motion on an arterial road when he tapped. Nothing in this record supports a recomputed waiting clock, and no false-arrival referral arises.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-03101", "EV-TRIP-03101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.arrived_at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace is complete and unimpaired for the tests this case turns on: 100.0% coverage, 99 fixes on a 10 second cadence, max_gap_sec 0.0 and gaps empty, both tracks present. No limb of POL-NS-08 - clock skew, trace gap, chat defect or fare defect - is engaged: the marker and the GPS fix agree to the second, there is no sampling gap inside the waiting window, the chat log's 2 messages match the trip record's chat_message_count of 2, and the charged line of SGD 4.50 equals platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd, so the POL-NS-08(d) reconciliation is clean. POL-NS-02's arrival test and POL-NS-01(c)'s dwell measurement can both be run on admissible fixes.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-03101", "EV-TRIP-03101", "EV-CHAT-03101", "EV-FARE-03101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08", "POL-NS-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider-exonerating clause POL-NS-04 cannot apply because its third limb fails affirmatively, even taking the rider's case at its highest. I accept that limbs (a) and (b) are made out: the rider sent a coordinating message at 17:06:00 ('coming down now') and the driver neither replied in chat within 120 seconds nor placed any in-app call, trip_record.in_app_calls being empty. But limb (c) requires the rider's device to be within the 100 m STANDARD rider presence radius for the majority of qualifying fixes across the waiting window, and rider_qualifying_fix_count is 0: every one of the rider's 71 fixes from 17:00:44 to 17:11:14 places the device between 672.4 m and 679.8 m from the pickup pin, with a mean of 675.9 m. All three limbs are required, so the clause leaves the fee undisturbed.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-03101", "EV-CHAT-03101", "EV-TRIP-03101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04", "POL-NS-11"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.mean_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-06, the shortfall route, is unavailable on this record. It refunds the fee only where the effective in-geofence dwell is shorter than the free waiting period in force; here the dwell is 410 seconds against 180 seconds, a 230 second surplus, so its premise is not met. Limb (i)'s advisory-based accumulation is likewise unavailable twice over: the trace shows a single in-geofence interval (run_count 1), so there is no second interval to sum, and the only advisory covering this pickup, EV-ADVIS-03101-01, is MISSING with weight 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT - I disclose that impairment expressly, and per POL-GEN-02 a MISSING artifact carries no fact at all, so no party can assert advisory accumulation from it. Nothing turns on it in any event, because the dwell already exceeds the minimum within one interval.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-03101", "EV-ADVIS-03101-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.limb.available",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's narrative does not survive his own device's trace. He says he was 'only a few minutes late' and 'came down', but his device never comes closer than 672.4 m to the pickup pin at any point in the recorded window and never enters the 100 m rider presence radius. The reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW therefore describes this trip accurately, and the rider's absence - not any premature departure by the driver - is what ended it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-03101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The failed-locate branch of POL-NS-01 does not apply, so the refund outcomes attached to it are not in play. This cancellation was recorded under RIDER_NO_SHOW, not DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE, and the driver's stationary fixes lie inside the 50 m arrival radius, so this is a case where the driver did arrive and did hold position. On that footing the four conjunctive limbs of POL-NS-01 are met and POL-NS-07 fixes the driver's payout, which is what the clause's own terms contemplate for a verified no-show.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-03101", "EV-GPS-03101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-07"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-07 fixes the money. POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, so the driver is compensated at 80 percent of the cancellation fee in force: 80 percent of SGD 4.50 is SGD 3.60, the exact figure the fare breakdown's own derived money block computes as driver_compensation under POL-NS-07. The fee line itself is sound - SGD 4.50 charged, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00 - and the driver's gross figure of SGD 6.61 is not the basis of the payout, the net figure is.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-03101", "EV-TRIP-03101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.driver_compensation",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The anti-farming check does not withhold the payout, and it is run only on the fields the policy names. The driver's no_show_terminations_30d is 2, below the absolute limb of 4, and 2 divided by completed_trips_30d of 63 is 0.032, below the rate limb of 0.08. Both limbs must trip and neither does. The lifetime prior_no_show_flags counter is not the trailing-30-day figure POL-NS-07 reads and I do not rely on it, or on any other context-only profile field, as a ground of decision.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-03101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No POL-NS-09 escalation trigger fires, so this case is decidable on the record rather than held. Confidence is not below the 0.70 floor because every artifact carrying a deciding fact here is COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0; no two admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence - the trip record and the GPS agree to the second; rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d are both 0, so limb (c) needs no review; the POL-NS-07 check does not trip and rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1, below the 3 that limb (d) requires; and nothing deciding this case is impaired under POL-NS-08(a) to (d).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-03101", "EV-TRIP-03101", "EV-RPROF-03101", "EV-DPROF-03101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The disposition follows from what the fee is and who filed. The rider filed this dispute and the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee stands on the ledger as CHARGED with no refund issued; under POL-GEN-03 NO_ACTION is party-relative and on a rider-filed dispute leaves that charge exactly as it is, while the outcome this case produces under POL-NS-07 is DRIVER_COMPENSATION of SGD 3.60, amount_sgd mirroring driver_compensation_sgd as POL-GEN-03 directs. The fee is not refunded and the driver is paid.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-03101", "EV-DPROF-03101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-NS-07"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.fee_charged",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
